WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.620
Boo! It's Halloween, guys!

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:08.360
According to a handful of polls, belief in ghosts may be

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:14.000
on the rise. A 2007 AP/Ipsos poll found
that 1/3 of American adults believed in

00:00:14.010 --> 00:00:19.680
ghosts. In a 2011 CBS News question, 40
percent said that they believed that

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.570
ghosts, or the spirits of the dead ,could
come back. Now it's half. Additionally, an

00:00:24.570 --> 00:00:29.670
October 2017 Chapman University poll
found that 52 percent believe in

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:34.079
hauntings. And belief in the paranormal
might even be more common than that! The

00:00:34.079 --> 00:00:38.729
Chapman University survey says that
nearly 75% of us believe in at least one

00:00:38.729 --> 00:00:43.260
of seven paranormal phenomena, like
extraterrestrials, clairvoyance, or

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:48.889
Bigfoot. And yet, Americans don't think
they're very superstitious. In an AP poll,

00:00:48.889 --> 00:00:53.459
79% of Republicans and Democrats said
they weren't superstitious. So how can

00:00:53.459 --> 00:00:58.379
Americans be skeptical and superstitious
at the same time? Maybe it's only a

00:00:58.379 --> 00:01:03.239
superstition when other people believe
it. As one Bigfoot hunter said: "Just

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:07.240
because I hunt Bigfoot doesn't mean I
believe everything I hear".

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:13.619
It appears that belief in ghosts is increasing. What
do you think? Let us know your comments.

00:01:13.619 --> 00:01:18.149
Also, let us know what other topics you'd
like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:18.149 --> 00:01:24.079
and be sure to like and subscribe for
more research and videos from AEI.

